WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.740
Hey, welcome back. This is day 22, I think, in

2
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:12.320
the

3
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.950
40 Days of Holiness campaign. So thankful that you're here today.

4
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.390
There's a really beautiful passage of scripture in Ephesians chapter 5.

5
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.020
So grab your notebook, workbook, and follow along there.

6
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.040
Take some notes and let's seek the Lord together in his Word.

7
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.810
All right? Ephesians chapter 5.

8
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.880
Let's start with verse 15. All right?

9
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.000
"Be very careful then how you live,

10
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.180
not as unwise but as wise." So I'm going to just point

11
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.140
out to you here that he's talking to Christians, all right, people in Ephesus that

12
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.900
are part of the church, so they're saved, and he's presenting two

13
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.000
contrasting ways they could approach life. Okay?

14
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.660
"Not as unwise but as wise, making the most of every

15
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:59.700
opportunity," wise, "because the days are evil." So he's contrasting

16
00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.640
people who go along with evil days versus make the most of their Christian life.

17
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.040
And then he says, "Therefore, do not be foolish, but understand what the Lord's

18
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.660
will is." So you could be foolish as a Christian, or you could understand the will

19
00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.580
of the Lord. And then he says something really interesting.

20
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.340
Today's metaphor for our time together

21
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.420
is, "Do not get drunk on wine, which leads to debauchery.

22
00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.500
Instead, be filled with the Spirit." Now, that is a

23
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.360
really odd comparison, isn't it? Being drunk with wine compared to

24
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.820
being filled with the Holy Spirit. Why would he do that?

25
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.420
Why would he compare and connect those two things?

26
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:37.660
Well,

27
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.260
here's why. And so today, I want to point out to you he's

28
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.400
talking about an issue of control.

29
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.560
So being drunk has a comparison with being filled

30
00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.100
with the Holy Spirit, and the key issue at stake is an

31
00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.100
issue of control. That these are both something where a

32
00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.360
person is being controlled by something

33
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.380
not in themselves, by something that is not their own will.

34
00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.660
It is their own will under the influence of something

35
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.620
else. Right? So if someone gets drunk, we say they are under the influence

36
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.440
of alcohol. And so if someone is filled with the Holy Spirit,

37
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.200
they are in a particular way under the influence

38
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.440
of the Holy Spirit in a way that is deeper and greater than

39
00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.420
they would've been before, even than these Christians were as Christians

40
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.880
in Ephesus. Now, I think this is very important.

41
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.520
He goes into a series of things in Greek.

42
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.640
You can't really see this in English necessarily, but in Greek it's like this.

43
00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.920
Big idea, be filled with the Holy Spirit.

44
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.860
And then he introduces a series of participles in Greek that are kind of like

45
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.520
sub-points underneath that. And he talks about the ways in which

46
00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.060
being filled with the Holy Spirit influences you.

47
00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.750
So he talks about speaking to one another in psalms, hymns, and

48
00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.730
spiritual songs. So there's a speaking.

49
00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.680
This control of the Holy Spirit, being filled with him,

50
00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.680
it influences your speaking. So it influences your speech and the

51
00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.680
way you use your speech and the way you speak to

52
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.580
one another. If you are a person who has a

53
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.160
tongue that is extra sharp or extra acidic or extra

54
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.160
sarcastic, maybe you need to deal with the issue of being

55
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.280
filled with the Holy Spirit and controlled by him in that way.

56
00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.880
So you yield that part of your body, like we talked about

57
00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:32.440
yesterday, to the Holy Spirit in a newer and deeper way.

58
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.890
So speaking to one another. Singing and making melody in your heart to the

59
00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.310
Lord, making music in your heart to God.

60
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.680
So it affects your speech, the way you speak to the

61
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.360
Lord, and your attitude toward him.

62
00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.780
By the way, does being drunk affect the way you speak? Oh, yeah. Yeah.

63
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.560
You ever met a mean drunk or a mad drunk or a sad drunk or a

64
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.459
liquid courage drunk? Right?

65
00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.100
Where they'll say anything to anybody because they've had a shot of tequila,

66
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.180
right? So, singing and making melody is another one.

67
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.840
Does drunkenness influence those things? Oh, absolutely.

68
00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.400
So does being filled and controlled by the Holy Spirit.

69
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.220
Always giving thanks for everything to the Lord.

70
00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.780
So it affects your attitudes to be filled with the Holy Spirit.

71
00:04:18.041 --> 00:04:20.661
Does being drunk affect your attitude? Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

72
00:04:20.721 --> 00:04:23.640
I had a neighbor that was a great guy, unless he was drinking.

73
00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.940
He was nice and he'd take my trash cans out for me before I even realized it was

74
00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.140
trash day and he'd have them out the night before.

75
00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.060
Cool guy, really nice, friendly, unless he'd been drinking and then we had a

76
00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.680
problem. All right? He was mean and nasty and argumentative and

77
00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.650
foul-mouthed. All these things got affected by what was controlling and

78
00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.680
influencing him. And the last one is submitting to one another in the fear of

79
00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.440
the Lord. So

80
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.570
here's what I want to say. The metaphor that the Spirit or

81
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.230
that God is giving us in his word today

82
00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.020
is that being filled with the Spirit, there's a new level

83
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.720
of holiness in our attitudes, actions, music, words,

84
00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.360
relationships. All of those things are brought to

85
00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:12.000
bear by a new level of control. It's

86
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:16.020
almost like being intoxicated. Now, I want to tell you one

87
00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.800
more thing that is important for you to understand in this metaphor, is

88
00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:20.160
that

89
00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.300
being drunk is not something you do one time and then you never have to do it

90
00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:29.160
again. It has to be maintained, right? You got to keep getting under the influence.

91
00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.420
You got to keep drinking to stay drunk.

92
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.200
In the same kind of way, it's almost like he says in Greek,

93
00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:39.420
"Be being filled." So not filled in the sense of a

94
00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.900
cup that sits there, but filled in the sense of a

95
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.820
conduit, of a channel, of a water pipe through which water

96
00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.420
is continually flowing. Be always filled.

97
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.920
Be always being filled is almost the way that it comes across.

98
00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.560
You got to maintain this. You got to maintain it.

99
00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.960
So if you are a Christian, there's a call God's sending

100
00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.360
out to you to be filled, to be always filled.

101
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.340
So filled that it controls you. So controlled that it

102
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.220
dictates and demonstrates and flows out in new holy life

103
00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.430
patterns of speech and attitude and thought and

104
00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.460
thanksgiving and relationships.

105
00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.460
So let me encourage you, this is our metaphor for today.

106
00:06:21.469 --> 00:06:25.430
Are you filled, influenced? Are you under the influence of

107
00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.030
the Holy Spirit?

108
00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:27.410
See you tomorrow.
